## 🏗️ Architecture Deep Dive

MIRA follows a **three-tier architecture**:

```mermaid
graph TB
    User[👤 User] -->|SSE/WebSocket| UI[Frontend - Flask UI]
    User -->|Voice| Voice[Voice Agent]
    
    UI -->|SSE| MCP[MCP Server :9000]
    Voice -->|Direct Import| Agent
    
    MCP -->|Orchestrates| Agent[Agent - LLM Orchestrator]
    MCP -->|Manages Plugins| Plugins[Plugin Manager]
    
    Agent -->|Calls| Tools[Tool Registry]
    Agent -->|Model Requests| LLM[LLM Backend<br/>Groq/Gemini/Ollama]
    
    Tools -->|Executes via| Connectors[Connectors]
    Tools -->|Extends via| Plugins
    
    Connectors -->|System APIs| System[System OS]
    Connectors -->|Vector Store| RAG[ChromaDB]
    Connectors -->|SQLite| DB[(Local DB)]
    
    style UI fill:#4a90e2
    style MCP fill:#e27d60
    style Agent fill:#85dcba
    style Tools fill:#e8a87c
    style Connectors fill:#c38d9e
    style RAG fill:#ffd700
```

### Layer 1: Frontend (UI)

**Location**: [ui/app.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/ui/app.py)

- Flask web server running on `http://localhost:5000`
- Serves HTML chat interface with real-time SSE updates
- **SSE Streaming**: Sends token-by-token reasoning and tool updates to the UI via `/api/stream`

**Key Routes**:
- `GET /` - Main chat interface
- `GET /api/stream` - [NEW] Server-Sent Events (SSE) for streaming agent reasoning
- `POST /api/reset` - Clear conversation history
- `GET /api/list-files` - List files in `SANDBOX/`
- `POST /api/read-file` - Read file content

### Layer 2: MCP Server (Orchestration)

**Location**: [mcp_server/server.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/mcp_server/server.py)

- WebSocket server on `ws://localhost:9000`
- **Plugin Manager**: Discovers and auto-loads plugins from the `plugins/` directory
- Manages Agent lifecycle and tool synchronization

**Key Actions**:
- `agent_invoke_stream` - [NEW] Invoke agent with SSE streaming events
- `plugin.install`, `plugin.list` - Manage dynamic capabilities
- `ping` - Health check
- `list_dir`, [read_file](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/ui/app.py#113-138), `add_event`, `list_events` - Direct MCP calls

### Layer 3: Agent (Intelligence)

**Location**: [agent/agent.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/agent/agent.py)

The **brain** of MIRA. Features:
1. **Loop Detection**: Automatically breaks infinite tool-call repetitions
2. **Robust Parsing**: Advanced brace-matching parser for tool calls
3. **Multi-Provider Rotation**: Smart fallback across 5+ providers in [model_adapter.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/agent/model_adapter.py)
4. **Autonomous Execution**: Detects when more steps are needed, continues until task completion

**Key Methods**:
- `Agent.handle_streaming(text, model)` - [NEW] Specialized entry point for UI updates
- `Agent._build_system_prompt()` - Creates core instruction set
- `Agent.reset()` - Resets internal state and loop detectors

