### 4. 🌐 Web & Search

**Connectors**: [search.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/mcp_server/connectors/search.py) · [web.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/mcp_server/connectors/web.py) · [firecrawl.py](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/mcp_server/connectors/firecrawl.py)

| Tool | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `search.duckduckgo` | Search the web with DuckDuckGo (no API key needed) |
| `search.news` | Search for latest news stories via DuckDuckGo |
| `web.fetch` | Fetch raw HTML from a URL |
| `web.read` | Extract clean article text from a URL (strips ads/clutter) |
| `web.summarize` | Fetch and LLM-summarize a URL |
| `firecrawl.scrape` | Scrape a single page → returns markdown (JS-rendered) |
| `firecrawl.crawl` | Crawl an entire website and save JSON to `SANDBOX/` |
| `firecrawl.map` | Discover all URLs on a website (no scraping) |
| `firecrawl.search` | Search the web and auto-scrape results into markdown |
| `firecrawl.search_cache` | Full-text search over all previously scraped pages (instant, offline) |
| `firecrawl.extract` | AI-powered structured data extraction by JSON schema |

> [!NOTE]
> **Search Decision Guide**:
> - `search.duckduckgo` — Fast, no-key-needed, returns snippets + links.
> - `web.read` — Read a single known article URL cleanly.
> - `firecrawl.scrape` — Heavy/JS sites needing full render. Requires Firecrawl on `localhost:3100`.


