## ⚙️ Setup & Configuration

### Prerequisites

- **Windows OS** (PowerShell required)
- **Python 3.12+**
- **Ollama** (for local LLM) OR **Groq API Key** (for cloud LLM)
- **Git** (optional, for cloning updates)

### Step 1: Environment Setup

```bash
# Navigate to project directory
cd C:\Users\lenovo\Downloads\MIRA-Deliverables\MIRA-Windows

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
venv\Scripts\activate

# [NEW] Install as editable package (PEP 517)
# This enables clean imports across the project without sys.path hacks
pip install -e .

# Install additional dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 2: Configure API Keys

Edit [.env](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/.env):

```env
# --- MULTI-PROVIDER ROTATION (MIRA SMART FALLBACK) ---
# MIRA automatically rotates between these 5 providers to avoid rate limits.
# Recommended: Get free keys for all of them to maximize RPM.

GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxx
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSyAxxx
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=csk_xxx       # cloud.cerebras.ai (30 RPM, legacy speed)
SAMBANOVA_API_KEY=xxx-xxx-xxx  # cloud.sambanova.ai
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-xxx   # openrouter.ai/keys (Free Llama 70B)

# Firecrawl Configuration (for web scraping tools)
FIRECRAWL_API_URL=http://localhost:3100

# SMTP Configuration (for email sending)
SMTP_USER=your.email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your_app_password_here
SMTP_SERVER=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587

# IMAP Configuration (for email reading)
IMAP_USER=your.email@gmail.com
IMAP_PASS=your_app_password_here
IMAP_SERVER=imap.gmail.com
```


> [!TIP]
> For Gmail, generate an App Password at [myaccount.google.com/apppasswords](https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords)

### Step 3: Choose LLM Backend

**Option A: Local (Ollama)**

```bash
# Install Ollama from https://ollama.ai

# Pull recommended model
ollama pull mistral:7b
```

**Option B: Cloud (Groq)**

- Sign up at [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com)
- Add `GROQ_API_KEY` to [.env](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/.env)

**Option C: Cloud (Gemini)**

- Get API key at [aistudio.google.com/app/apikey](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)
- Add `GEMINI_API_KEY` to [.env](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/.env)
- Supports Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite (best free tier: 15 RPM, 1000 requests/day)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Recommended Model**: `mistral:7b` or higher (7B+ parameters)  
> Small models like `qwen2.5:3b` cause hallucinations. See [RECOMMENDED_MODELS.md](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/RECOMMENDED_MODELS.md).

### Step 4: Launch MIRA

**Standard Mode (Web UI)**:
```bash
# Run both MCP server and UI
run.bat
```

This starts:
1. MCP Server on `ws://localhost:9000`
2. Flask UI on `http://localhost:5000`

**Voice Mode**:
```bash
# Interactive voice assistant
run_voice.bat
```

**Mobile Access (via ngrok)**:
```bash
# Expose UI publicly for mobile testing
run_with_ngrok.bat
```

See [NGROK_SETUP.md](file:///C:/Users/lenovo/Downloads/MIRA-Deliverables/MIRA-Windows/NGROK_SETUP.md) for details.

